infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title The real production choice: loss vs duplicates
  desc Exactly-once delivery is impossible, so the contract you pick trades a lost message against a duplicate one
  compares
    - label At-most-once
      children
        - label Send once, never retry
          desc No duplicates by construction
        - label Can lose messages
          desc A dropped network packet is gone forever
        - label Ack BEFORE processing
          desc A crash after ack loses the message
        - label Use for metrics and logs
          desc Loss is acceptable, never for money
    - label At-least-once
      children
        - label Retry until consumer acks
          desc The production default in SQS, RabbitMQ, Kafka
        - label Can deliver 2+ times
          desc A lost ack forces a redelivery
        - label Ack AFTER processing
          desc Plus a dedup check absorbs the duplicate
        - label Use for payments and orders
          desc Loss unacceptable, duplicates fixable
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
